<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-3353] IGFS: Out-of-igfs-space exception is lost.</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-3353</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Two problems with space calculation:&lt;br/&gt;
1) If out-of-space exception is thrown, there is no guarantees that relevant output stream will notice it, because &lt;tt&gt;onDone()&lt;/tt&gt; method removes relevant future.&lt;br/&gt;
2) Currently if max space is set to zero, we attempt to calculate it on our own, using &lt;tt&gt;0.8 * heapSize&lt;/tt&gt; metrics. This is terribly wrong for OFFHEAP cache. &lt;/p&gt;</description>
